},"created_at":"2026-10-12T11:33:31Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T11:33:31Z","body":"## AI Security Review\n**Experiment condition:** C\n**Automated operational score:** 85/100 — LOW — APPROVE\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **MEDIUM · POLICY_OR_COMPLIANCE · Subnet lacks NSG association (NET-001 violation)**\n  - Category rationale: Policy NET-001 requires all subnets to have an NSG associated. The Terraform configuration defines azurerm_subnet.subnet but includes no azurerm_subnet_network_security_group_association resource or inline NSG reference linking nsg-demo-ai to subnet-demo. The NSG exists in nsg.tf but is unattached to the subnet, leaving it without effective NSG enforcement at the subnet level despite the NSG resource being defined. The Checkov finding CKV2_AZURE_31 on azurerm_subnet.subnet corroborates this gap.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_subnet.subnet in terraform/network.tf defines the subnet with no nsg_id or inline NSG reference. No azurerm_subnet_network_security_group_association resource appears in any supplied file. azurerm_network_security_group.nsg is defined in terraform/nsg.tf but contains no subnet_id or association reference. Checkov CKV2_AZURE_31 flags azurerm_subnet.subnet in /network.tf.\n  - Analysis: The subnet azurerm_subnet.subnet (subnet-demo, 10.0.1.0/24) is defined in network.tf without an associated Network Security Group. Although azurerm_network_security_group.nsg (nsg-demo-ai) is defined in nsg.tf with deny-all inbound and outbound rules, no azurerm_subnet_network_security_group_association resource exists anywhere in the supplied configuration to bind the NSG to the subnet. Azure applies NSG rules only when the NSG is explicitly associated with a subnet or NIC; an unassociated NSG provides no protection at the subnet boundary.\n  - Impact: Without an NSG association, the subnet boundary is governed only by Azure's default network policy (default deny inbound from internet, default allow VNet-to-VNet, default allow outbound). The explicit deny-all rules in nsg-demo-ai are not enforced at the subnet level, creating a gap between the intended security posture and the deployed posture. If any resource is deployed into this subnet, traffic control relies solely on NIC-level NSGs or Azure defaults rather than the configured subnet NSG.\n  - Recommendation: Add an azurerm_subnet_network_security_group_association resource to associate azurerm_network_security_group.nsg with azurerm_subnet.subnet:\n\nresource \"azurerm_subnet_network_security_group_association\" \"subnet_nsg\" {\n  subnet_id                 = azurerm_subnet.subnet.id\n  network_security_group_id = azurerm_network_security_group.nsg.id\n}\n\n### Policy mappings\n- **NET-001** — All subnets must have a Network Security Group (NSG) associated. (finding F-001)\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6123430126/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gi